      {title:'Postharvest condition is linked to identity and location',body:'Record the dry-room rack or location, supplied environmental information and observed product condition for the correct identified lot. One nonuniform rack or suspect container is documented at its actual scope rather than generalized automatically to the entire room.',references:['REF-POSTHARVEST-001']},
      {title:'Uncertainty stays visible',body:'If root cause, final disposition, release status or a quantity discrepancy remains unresolved, state that directly. Technician I should not convert an unresolved condition into a guessed explanation or release decision simply to create a clean handoff.',references:['REF-MHRA-GXP-DATA-INTEGRITY']},
      {title:'Receiving records close the transition',body:'The handoff should allow the receiving role to connect source material, harvest output, destination, quantity, hold status, condition note, actions already taken, escalation and next required action. This closes the operational transition without erasing the open issues that still need qualified review.',references:['REF-GS1-GLOBAL-TRACEABILITY','REF-MHRA-GXP-DATA-INTEGRITY']}
